// Auscultation preset (brief B27): an ordinary ECG with the heart sounds of a valve, shunt or
// ventricular disorder. Timing rules and their sources are in docs/research/heart-sounds.md; every
// number of the sound model is documented in crates/heartsim-ecg/src/auscultation.rs.
Scenario(
    format_version: 1,
    id: "heart_failure_s3",
    title: "Heart failure with a third heart sound (S3 gallop)",
    description: "Sinus rhythm at 92 bpm in a dilated, failing left ventricle: a low third sound follows S2 in early diastole.",
    tier: Template,
    anatomy: "default",
    seed: 42,
    notes: Some("An S3 is a low-pitched sound about 120 to 200 ms after A2, at the end of rapid ventricular filling, when blood entering a dilated, stiff ventricle is checked abruptly. It does not need an atrial contraction, so it persists in atrial fibrillation. In an adult it points to systolic heart failure or volume overload; in children, young adults and pregnancy it can be normal.\nOn the lane: S1, S2, then a small slow wave labelled S3 in early diastole. Listen with the bell at the apex in the left lateral position.\nIn a breathless patient an S3 makes heart failure much more likely, but its absence does not exclude it. The ECG here is plain sinus rhythm: the ECG is not diagnostic of heart failure.\nDifferential: split S2, opening snap of mitral stenosis (higher pitched and earlier), S4 (before S1).\nThe sounds are a synthesised model, not a recording: timing follows the cited sources, pitch and loudness are designed. The lane under the strip shows the trace; pick a slower speed to hear the intervals stretch."),
    confused_with: ["lvh_s4", "summation_gallop", "mitral_stenosis_sinus"],
    references: [
        "MSD Manual Professional Version: Cardiac auscultation (Approach to the cardiac patient), msdmanuals.com.",
        "Nemani L, Pechetty S. Additional heart sounds, part 1. Indian J Cardiovasc Dis Women (ijcdw.org).",
        "Williams. In: Walker HK, Hall WD, Hurst JW, eds. Clinical Methods, 3rd ed. Butterworths 1990, ch. 25 (NCBI Bookshelf NBK344).",
        "Wang CS et al. Does this dyspneic patient in the emergency department have congestive heart failure? JAMA 2005;294:1944-1956.",
    ],
    expected: Some(ExpectedFindings(
        hr_bpm: (60.0, 100.0),
        pr_ms: Some((120.0, 200.0)),
        qrs_ms: Some((70.0, 110.0)),
        axis_deg: Some((-30.0, 90.0)),
        extra_sounds: Some([S3]),
        murmurs: Some([]),
        s2_split: Some(Physiological),
    )),
    auscultation: (s3: true),
    timing: TimingParams(
        sinus: SinusParams(rate_bpm: 92.0),
    ),
)
